                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa15e853-d85a-3971-9c86-4eb17395c8f8",
                                        "entry_id": "896ca3dc-9214-3537-8be8-f4da2234edef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anatomie, überkommenDer Mythos Jungfernhäutchen. In: emma.de, 6. September 2010 (2. Januar 2012)Nichts zu reißen. In: badische-zeitung.de,Ratgeber, Gesundheit & Ernährung dünnhäutige Membran, welche die Vaginalöffnung einer Frau umrahmen beziehungsweise mehr oder weniger bedecken kann"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "28. Dezember 2011] (28. Dezember 2011)"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d50dc15f-1194-4f43-92a9-bcf091fb7adb",
                                                "sense_id": "aa15e853-d85a-3971-9c86-4eb17395c8f8",
                                                "text": "„Susanne Leimstoll: Aber was ist das für eine Ehre, die von einem Jungfernhäutchen abhängt?.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed4b457e-9e8f-4525-a58c-76f00d9eee51",
                                                "sense_id": "aa15e853-d85a-3971-9c86-4eb17395c8f8",
                                                "text": "„Was seine eigene Frau betrifft, so war sie, wie ich später herausfand, nur insofern Invalide, als ihr Jungfernhäutchen noch intakt war.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5616d874-ce73-48ca-ada3-c96796a58085",
                                                "sense_id": "aa15e853-d85a-3971-9c86-4eb17395c8f8",
                                                "text": "„Ich denke an ihren Lieblingswitz, den mit dem Meterpreis für Jungfernhäutchen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "27f35c08-63a6-4bb7-b492-76a0df07e3d9",
                        "source_entry_id": "abb5e353-f2d7-3382-a69f-99b5f7856947",
                        "source_sense_id": "fc71ab3c-c41c-3c43-ad0e-964fc83a52bb",
                        "source_sense_description": "vlies",
                        "target_lang_word": "hymen",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hymen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee000452-ad79-3a02-bfdd-98c455e24411",
                                        "entry_id": "89ab4763-00a2-31da-ae62-beba4de406e2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A membrane which completely or partially occludes the vaginal opening in human females."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5b5c9af-7071-3e9d-9e73-bc9a805e9eb2",
                                        "entry_id": "89ab4763-00a2-31da-ae62-beba4de406e2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Marriage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da5cdd26-c7e7-43e4-ba84-02445e06b4bb",
                                                "sense_id": "b5b5c9af-7071-3e9d-9e73-bc9a805e9eb2",
                                                "text": "I would for ever baniſh from my thoughts—I will obey the firſt ſummons that proclaims you a happy wife.—On my devoted head may every miſery, reſulting from an ill-fated marriage, have juſtly been exhauſted. On your propitious hymen may ſmiling peace, domeſtic harmony, and mutual love, for ever wait; and time alone diſſolve the tender union!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f07146f3-2c0f-4d6e-aad2-34b36162618b",
                                                "sense_id": "b5b5c9af-7071-3e9d-9e73-bc9a805e9eb2",
                                                "text": "Fanny read to herself that \"it was with infinite concern the newspaper had to announce to the world, a matrimonial fracas in the family of Mr. R. of Wimpole Street; the beautiful Mrs. R. whose name had not long been enrolled in the lists of hymen, and who had promised to become so brilliant a leader in the fashionable world, having quitted her husband's roof in company with the well known and captivating Mr. C. the intimate friend and associate of Mr. R. and it was not known, even to the editor of the newspaper, whither they were gone.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "15119577-dc31-416b-b7ac-ebb86e89d937",
                        "source_entry_id": "abb5e353-f2d7-3382-a69f-99b5f7856947",
                        "source_sense_id": "fc71ab3c-c41c-3c43-ad0e-964fc83a52bb",
                        "source_sense_description": "vlies",
                        "target_lang_word": "maidenhead",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "maidenhead",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb64b3f7-5a9b-3d11-b4cb-ae0dda45e901",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb04c93-9051-32e0-bb7d-6e054846faa1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The hymen."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "literally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a98f0092-8b6a-4a06-b990-99eed68879e1",
                                                "sense_id": "cb64b3f7-5a9b-3d11-b4cb-ae0dda45e901",
                                                "text": "Ay, the heads of the maids, or their maidenheads; take it in what sense thou wilt."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                        "entry_id": "fbb04c93-9051-32e0-bb7d-6e054846faa1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Virginity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "metonymically",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c741aa8-fd5d-4b07-aabf-b28b546d16d5",
                                                "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                                "text": "Put in but little Silver or Gold, for if you do, you quite spoil the Compoſition ; but inſtead thereof, add of Tradeſmens Bills for Cloaths, to the Value of 100 l. [¶] Laſtly, Take away the Girl's Maidenhead, and then the Compoſition is fit for Uſe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6558f39-0d3a-4bed-922b-1770b2bc2d2b",
                                                "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                                "text": "Gallants, a bashful poet bids me say,\nHe's come to lose his maidenhead to-day.\nBe not too fierce; for he's but green of age,\nAnd ne'er, till now, debauch'd upon the stage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c27c6814-eabe-4ca7-ae07-e6e0d52fe7c8",
                                                "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                                "text": "My lord,[…]/ I brought you nothing else it may be said / But faith and nakedness and maidenhead."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4cb0664-ca39-4dab-b924-38924d944746",
                                                "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                                "text": "She prayed to Pallas, and by her help escaped from him in the form of a crow, rejoicing more to keep her maidenhead white under the blackness of the feathers than to lose it and be adorned with the fairest pearls."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31050c70-14dd-42a9-9ea1-86304f88e8cf",
                                                "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                                "text": "So the reference to the plucking of the ginger flower is again an indirect allusion to the taking of the girl's maidenhead ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f33fe61-a9b2-403d-83b1-31352ceaf2be",
                                                "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                                "text": "The gender reversals that pervade this play continue mischievously in the man's maidenhead being the undisclosed secret."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cd68c80-10b1-4cca-b2f0-9d7ae8bba318",
                                                "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                                "text": "“[…] He said that Katheryn told him he should have her maidenhead, though it be painful to her. I told him to be gone with his empty promises of marriage. But I doubt not that Mr. Mannox has known her intimately.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e227ab9f-5611-4881-821f-24677889044e",
                                                "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                                "text": "[…] a young virgin makes an even trade of her maidenhead for a hat that she desires. She negotiates with the haberdasher, who originally stipulated for her maidenhead plus a crown […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "244faade-30a5-457e-a655-48725cf56175",
                                                "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                                "text": "The penis imagery becomes apparent: the nails are 'blunt' and 'large', designed to push through the fair skin in body parts (feet, hands) that had earlier been described in erotically-charged language. As if losing his maidenhead, Christ's body 'bursts' when entered, bringing forth a gush of blood that mars his white (womanly) skin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83efbae2-ab73-4ce9-b162-b65725d7d58c",
                                                "sense_id": "adcc23fc-c0b5-32d2-a55c-6dab489fd7be",
                                                "text": "Almost immediately afterwards, Scanlan discovered that the marriage was legal; Ellie was his wife. He began to feel that he had paid an exceptionally high price for his maidenhead."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "37771477-4ff9-4b8a-b2b4-5908d3fd3204",
                        "source_entry_id": "abb5e353-f2d7-3382-a69f-99b5f7856947",
                        "source_sense_id": "fc71ab3c-c41c-3c43-ad0e-964fc83a52bb",
                        "source_sense_description": "vlies",
